# CI-BOSS-CONSUMERS-01 — independent static acceptance of V2

The external five-test candidate is accepted statically, pending native execution. Exact ed95 original cohesion19/5 failure logs and source hashes are retained and independently checked. Main five files remain original; all11 frozen P9 files remain unchanged.

This is a current-content test migration, not assertion-equivalent P9 refactoring. Old single-loot and generic mini-explosion positives conflict with adopted Bell content. Their replacements observe four real physical coin sprites, actual bound finite articulated death, one impact/final event and no duplicate generic layer. Immediate seal/completion and pre-impact rejection are separated from later actual entitlement and pickup. Original wall,anchor,input,resource,duplicate-claim,ability,transition and fatal-tie intentions remain. Current40HP projectile cases preserve all8 actual firing positions and require exactly one tuned damage; explicitly historical16/36 cases remain unchanged.

Existing campaign fixture still serves7 real consumers. Bell and Pressure waits read their own Definitions and actual owner clocks, with bounded extra frames inside unchanged suite budgets. The shared collector reads actual units, uses the original App pickup/wallet/ledger admission and retries each claim to prove rejection. It does not grant balances, fabricate claims or advance Boss clocks. Its player positioning is explicit and is not natural traversal proof.

ReviewV1 manually called visual._process(0); this could hide broken automatic processing. V2 instead observes after natural node processing via process_frame and a zero-duration SceneTreeTimer. OriginalV1 remains archived. V2 patch SHA462cade8b900c72e1ab78826ad011dcd058f1d20a4755049998e14b9150f7e6c.

